CHECK:BIT_MACRO: Prefer using the BIT macro
#75: FILE: drivers/iommu/arm-smmu.c:311:
+#define ARM_SMMU_OPT_INST_AS_DATA      (1 << 1)

Defines like: 1 << <digit> could be BIT(digit).
The BIT() macro is defined via include/linux/bits.h::

  #define BIT(nr)         (1UL << (nr))

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'smmu->version == ARM_SMMU_V2'
#91: FILE: drivers/iommu/arm-smmu.c:1105:
+		if ((smmu->version == ARM_SMMU_V2) &&
+		    (smmu->options & ARM_SMMU_OPT_INST_AS_DATA))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

